<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Aulikara dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">400 CE – 545 CE (approx.) · capital Dashapura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Malwa dynasty of Dashapura whose king Yashodharman claimed victory over the Huns and boasted of ruling from the Himalaya to the ocean.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Aulikaras ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandsaur">Dashapura</a>, modern Mandsaur in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, from around 400, at first as allies or feudatories of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>. Their early kings, such as Naravarman and Bandhuvarman, are known from inscriptions dated in the Malava era.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandsaur">Mandsaur</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> weavers' inscription records how a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> of weavers migrated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> to Dashapura and built a Sun temple in 436, restoring it in 473, a vivid picture of guild life in a prosperous city. Around 528 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasodharman">Yashodharman</a> set up victory pillars at Sondani near Mandsaur, claiming to have defeated the Hun ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihirakula">Mihirakula</a> and to rule lands never held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Guptas</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasodharman">Yashodharman's</a> dominion seems to have collapsed after his death, and the dynasty disappears from the record by the mid-6th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kalachuris-of-mahishmati">Kalachuris of Mahishmati</a> and other powers.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 400 CE – 545 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:67.66%;width:2.89%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 CE – 545 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dashapura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Naravarman, Bandhuvarman, Yashodharman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Aulikaras, Kingdom of Yashodharman</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=472&amp;focus=aulikara-dynasty" aria-label="Aulikara dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6813 1334 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Aulikara dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7362 1550h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7133 1590h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7133 1590h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=472&amp;focus=aulikara-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

